#: Volumes.md:1
msgid "Calculating the number of atoms/average CV in a part of the cell"
msgstr "Cell の一部の原子数・CV 平均"

#: Volumes.md:3
msgid ""
"There are times when you want to study how many atoms are in a particular "
"part of the simulation cell. For example, you might want to investigate how "
"many gas atoms are within one of the pores of a zeolite. Alternatively, you "
"might be interested in the number of ions that have penetrated into the "
"inner envelope of a membrane. It is relatively easy to calculate such CVs in"
" PLUMED. For example, if you want to calculate the number of atoms that are "
"within a sphere with radius 1.0 nm around atom 1 you can use an input "
"something like this:"
msgstr ""
"Zeolite 孔の Gas 原子や Membrane 内に入った Ion の数などを調べる場合があります。原子1の周囲1.0 nm 球の数なら、"

#: Volumes.md:21
msgid ""
"This input is relatively simple and illustrates the procedure that PLUMED "
"follows in calculating this quantity pretty clearly."
msgstr "単純で、計算手順も明確です。"

#: Volumes.md:23
msgid ""
"A vector `sp` is calculated. Each element in this vector is between 0 and 1 "
"and the $i$th element is one if atom $i$ is in the region of interest."
msgstr "`sp` Vector を計算する。0〜1で、$i$ 番目は原子 $i$ が領域内なら1。"

#: Volumes.md:24
msgid "The elements of the vector are all added together."
msgstr "全成分を足す。"

#: Volumes.md:26
msgid ""
"Step 2 in this procedure is fixed but there are a variety of differnt ways "
"of completing step 1 as there are a variety of ways of defining the region "
"of interest. The particular methods that are currently available are:"
msgstr "2は固定ですが、領域定義の1には複数の方法があります。"

#: Volumes.md:29
msgid ""
"INSPHERE - calculate whether atoms are within a spherical region centered on"
" a particular atom."
msgstr "INSPHERE：特定原子を中心とする球内か判定する。"

# 原文の y_u の終了ドル記号欠落を補った。座標と数式の内容は保持した。
#: Volumes.md:30
msgid ""
"AROUND - calcualte the vector $(x,y,x)$ connecting each atom to a user-"
"specified atom that is at the origin. Then determine if $x_l < x < x_u$, "
"$y_l < y < y_u$ and $z_l < z < z_u$, where $x_l$, $x_u$, $y_l$, $y_u, $z_l$ "
"and $z_u$ are user specified parameters."
msgstr ""
"AROUND：指定原子を原点に各原子への $(x,y,x)$ を求め、$x_l < x < x_u$、$y_l < y < y_u$、$z_l < z "
"< z_u$ を判定する。$x_l$、$x_u$、$y_l$、$y_u$、$z_l$、$z_u$ は指定パラメータ。"

#: Volumes.md:31
msgid ""
"INCYLINDER - calculate whether atoms are within a cylindrical region that "
"has its long axis aligned with the $x$, $y$ or $z$ axis of the lab frame and"
" that is centerd on a particular atom."
msgstr "INCYLINDER：特定原子を中心、Lab の $x$・$y$・$z$ 軸方向の円柱内か判定する。"

#: Volumes.md:32
msgid ""
"CAVITY - calculate whether atoms are within a orthrhombic box whose "
"orientation and size is determined based on the position of four atoms."
msgstr "CAVITY：4原子から配向・大きさを定める直方体内か判定する。"

#: Volumes.md:33
msgid ""
"TETRAPORE - calculate whether atoms are within a orthrhombic box whose "
"orientation and size is determined based on the position of four atoms (the "
"calculation of the box is done differently to the way it is done with "
"CAVITY)."
msgstr "TETRAPORE：4原子から別の方法で直方体を定める。"

#: Volumes.md:34
msgid ""
"INENVELOPE - use kernel density estimation to calculate the density of a "
"particular atom type. Then for each of the atoms, $i$, in a second "
"(different) set to the one that was used to calculate the density determine "
"if they are in a region where the density of the first atom type is large. "
"This action could be used to determine whether ions are in a membrane."
msgstr ""
"INENVELOPE：ある原子種の密度を KDE で求め、別集合の各原子 $i$ が高密度領域にあるか判定する。Membrane 内の Ion "
"などに使える。"

#: Volumes.md:36
msgid "Using FIXEDATOM"
msgstr "FIXEDATOM の使用"

#: Volumes.md:38
msgid ""
"You will notice that when we use these commands for calculating the number "
"of atoms a part of the box there is always at least one atom that defines "
"the position of the origin. We do not use the positions that are calculated "
"from the MD code directly and instead calculate the position of the atom of "
"interest with respect to some other atom. Calculating these vectors "
"connecting pairs of atoms is essential. If we were to use the positions that"
" are passed from the MD code directly our CV would not be translationally "
"invariant. In other words, if we use the position that are passed from the "
"MD code when the position of the center of mass of the atoms changes the "
"values of the CV changes."
msgstr ""
"必ず少なくとも1原子を原点にし、MD の絶対位置でなく原子間 Vector を使います。そうしなければ並進不変でなく、系の Center of Mass"
" が移るだけで CV が変わります。"

#: Volumes.md:43
msgid ""
"Using the position of atom 1 as the position of the ORIGIN as I did above "
"might be useful in some cases. If you want to look at what is going on in a "
"particular part of the cell it is usually simpler to define a virtual atom "
"at the origin using FIXEDATOM like this:"
msgstr "原子1を原点にしてもよいですが、Cell の特定領域なら FIXEDATOM で原点を作る方が簡単です。"

#: Volumes.md:53
msgid ""
"As PBCs are applied on the distances calculated in the action `sp` using the"
" FIXEDATOM `f` at (0,0,0) ensures that the sphere is centered on the center "
"of the simulation cell."
msgstr "`sp` の距離には PBC が働くので、(0,0,0) の FIXEDATOM `f` で Cell 中心に球を置けます。"

#: Volumes.md:56
msgid "Calculating the average value of a CV in a region"
msgstr "領域内 CV の平均"

#: Volumes.md:58
msgid ""
"Methods for using the functionality discussed above to calculate the average"
" value of an order parameter in a particular part of the box are discussed "
"at length in [this tutorial "
"paper](https://pubs.acs.org/doi/10.1021/acs.jpcb.5c07562). The paper also "
"discusses how to ensure that such calculations run quickly."
msgstr ""
"[この Tutorial 論文](https://pubs.acs.org/doi/10.1021/acs.jpcb.5c07562) が Order "
"Parameter の領域平均と高速化を詳しく扱います。"

#: Volumes.md:61
msgid "Conclusions"
msgstr "結論"

#: Volumes.md:63
msgid ""
"The functionality described above can be used to calculate the average value"
" of any quantity in a region of interest. It will also work with CVs such as"
" LOCAL_Q6 or the LOCAL_AVERAGE of a symmetry function. Furthermore, even in "
"these cases the task list is optimised so that CVs that do not contribute to"
" the final CV value are not computed."
msgstr ""
"任意量、LOCAL_Q6、Symmetry Function の LOCAL_AVERAGE にも使えます。寄与しない CV を計算しないよう Task"
" List も最適化します。"
